/apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:58:    return turns;\n./tests/service/client/create-project-modal.test.ts:81:  it('TC-6.1a cancel project creation returns to a stable project index', () => {\n./tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts:88:  it('TC-1.1a returns shell HTML for authenticated project route', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts:174:  it('returns the authenticated user from /auth/me', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts:574:          turns: [],\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:162:| Get project shell data | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project identity plus project shell summaries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:164:In Epic 1, the project shell read path returns all process summaries needed to render and validate project-level process selection. The selected process is derived from the current browser route and matched against the returned `processes.items` collection. The shell read path may also return section-level error states for `processes`, `artifacts`, or `sourceAttachments` without failing the entire project-shell response when project identity and access still succeed. This story does not add a separate single-process read endpoint or a server-persisted selected-process write path.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:166:At Story 3 boundary, this is the first story that returns populated shell-section envelopes and section-level error states. Earlier stories may open the shell successfully without yet owning full summary population semantics.\n./tests/service/server/local-provider-adapter.test.ts:142:  it('hydrateEnvironment fails fast when a source clone returns an error', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/local-provider-adapter.test.ts:185:  it('executeScript runs