entries(args.archiveTurnsByProcessId ?? {})) {\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2421:        [...turns].sort((left, right) => left.turnIndex - right.turnIndex),\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3261:    turns: DerivedTurn[];\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3266:      args.turns\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3277:    const turns = [...(this.archiveTurnsByProcessId.get(args.processId) ?? [])].sort(\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3281:      items: turns,\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3288:      turns: paginated.items,\n./tests/service/server/provider-adapter-registry.test.ts:64:  it('returns the supplied adapter for any providerKind', () => {\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/00-foundation.md:106:| Get authenticated user | GET | `/auth/me` | Returns the current authenticated user or 401 if not authenticated |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/00-foundation.md:107:| Sign out authenticated user | POST | `/auth/logout` | Ends the current authenticated session and returns the browser to a signed-out state |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/00-foundation.md:108:| List accessible projects | GET | `/api/projects` | Returns the projects the current user can access |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/00-foundation.md:110:| Get project shell data | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project identity plus project shell summaries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/00-foundation.md:150:| `X-CSRF-Token` header | string | yes | Browser returns the shell bootstrap CSRF token on `POST /auth/logout` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/decision-memo.md:46:| Project shell partial failures | Use one aggregated project-shell bootstrap endpoint that returns per-section envelopes: `processes`, `artifacts`, and `sourceAttachments` each carry `status`, `items`, and optional `error`; return HTTP `200` when project identity/access succeeds, and reserve request failure codes for auth/access/not-found failures | Lock now | This is the cleanest way to satisfy the epic's partial-failure requirements without forcing client fan-out. It should be documented as a design-time clarification/deviation from the epic's simpler array-only contract. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:5:The client work is intentionally lighter than the process surface work. Review has no websocket subscription, no same-session action reconciliation, no live envelope. A durable bootstrap returns the workspace; reload replays the bootstrap; one HTTP request per navigation. What the client gains instead is surface richness — markdown rendering container, Mermaid hydration, version switching, package member navigation, and the single-action export trigger — but all of that sits on straightforward fetch-and-render plumbing.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:83:- `patchReviewTarget` — used when a version or member switch response returns a new target (keeps bootstrap context intact, replaces only the target and selection)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:120:The `getReviewWorkspace` call drives the initial bootstrap. `getArtifactReview` and `getPackageReview` are the targeted in-page switches (version switching within an artifact, member switching within a package) — they return just the target-level payload without re-fetching the entire workspace envelope. `exportPackage` is a POST that returns the export response metadata (phase 1 of the two-phase export flow); the user's browser then GETs `response.downloadUrl` to stream the `.mpkz` bytes (phase 2). The `getReviewWorkspace` call is not invoked from `exportPackage` — phase 2 is a direct anchor navigation to the signed download URL.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:276:| TC-6.2c | revoked access blocks direct URL | `tests/service/client/review-workspace-page.test.ts` | bootstrap returns 403 | route-level unavailable state renders |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:507:- **Two-phase flow**: phase 1 returns JSON metadata; phase 2 is a direct anchor navigation to the signed URL. The client's `review-workspace-api.ts` handles only phase 1. Phase 2 is the user clicking the rendered `<a href>` — no client-side `fetch` is involved\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:509:- **Expired URL handling**: if the user waits past `expiresAt` and clicks the download link, the server returns 404 at phase 2. The client has no direct signal from that 404 (the browser handles the failed navigation). The user re-clicks the export button to re-trigger phase 1 and get a fresh URL\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:521:| TC-5.3a | export failure does not close review | `tests/service/client/export-trigger.test.ts` | API returns 503 | failure affordance renders; package review panel remains operational |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:522:| TC-5.3b | expired export requires re-export | `tests/service/client/export-trigger.test.ts` | user clicks export twice; first response expires, second returns fresh | both clicks POST; second click renders fresh download link |\n./tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts:308:    turns: DerivedTurn[];\n./tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts:313:      turns: [],\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:100:**AC-1.4:** Authenticated project surfaces provide a sign-out action that ends the current session, returns the user to a signed-out state, and blocks access to project data until the user signs in again.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:105:  - Then: The platform ends the current session and returns the user to a signed-out state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:122:| Get authenticated user | GET | `/auth/me` | Returns the current authenticated user or 401 if not authenticated |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:123:| Sign out authenticated user | POST | `/auth/logout` | Ends the current authenticated session and returns the browser to a signed-out state |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:124:| List accessible projects | GET | `/api/projects` | Returns the projects the current user can access |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:125:| Get project shell data | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project identity plus project shell summaries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/01-authenticated-project-entry.md:150:`POST /auth/logout` returns `200` with a logout redirect payload after the authenticated session has been invalidated successfully.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/02-project-creation-and-open.md:61:  - Then: No project is created and the user returns to the project index unchanged\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/02-project-creation-and-open.md:97:**AC-6.1:** Canceling project creation or process creation creates no partial record and returns the user to a stable prior surface.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/02-project-creation-and-open.md:102:  - Then: No project record is created and the user returns to the project index\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/02-project-creation-and-open.md:116:| Get project shell data | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project identity plus project shell summaries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/02-project-creation-and-open.md:158:**Success response:** `POST /api/projects` returns `201` with a `Project Shell Response` body for the newly created project. On initial create, each section envelope returns an empty `items` array with `status: empty`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design.md:43:| Optional `processId` on the shell route implied `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` in the error table, but AC-6.2b requires the shell to remain usable when the selected process is missing | Query parameter contract, AC-6.2b | Aggregated shell bootstrap returns `200` for accessible projects and the client clears invalid process selection route state after comparing against `processes.items`; `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` remains reserved for dedicated process resources | Resolved — clarified |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design.md:98:The route returns a single `ProjectShellResponse`, but each section reader is a\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design.md:172:The projection returns:\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design.md:255:| `/projects` | Fastify shell route | Returns authenticated shell HTML or redirects to sign-in |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design.md:256:| `/projects/:projectId` | Fastify shell route | Returns authenticated shell HTML or project unavailable/auth redirect |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/tech-design.md:290:1. The shell bootstrap still returns `200` for an accessible project, and the\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:48:  userId: 'workos-user-turns-1',\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:49:  workosUserId: 'workos-user-turns-1',\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:166:describe('turn derivation service and route', () => {\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:167:  it('TC-4.1a turns derived from archive', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:180:      turns: [\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:215:      turns: [],\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:239:      turns: [\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:303:      turns: [\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:352:    const turns = await service.rebuildTurns({ projectId, processId });\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:354:    expect(turns).toEqual([\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:378:  it('turn-cache rebuild preserves stable turn provenance for derived views', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts:425:      throw new Error('Expected the initial rebuild to produce two turns.');\n./tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts:506:  ])('TC-5.3b returns REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND when the signed export URL token is $label', async ({\n./tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:900:  it('TC-4.1a returns informing source provenance', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:952:  it('TC-4.2a returns receiving source provenance', async () => {\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:103:| 19 | `story-continue` envelope returns `continuationHandle: null` on follow-up pass | **OPEN (minor)** | At 2026-04-23 ~11:20Z, Story 1 `story-continue` finished `ready-for-verification` cleanly, but the result envelope's `continuationHandle` field is null. The codex session underneath the continue call is obviously still valid (the continue succeeded against the same `019db9dc-dacb-76f3-b2d3-56a6594da7bb` handle), the CLI just doesn't echo it back. Orchestrator workaround: continue using the last known handle from the log's `Current Continuation Handles` section — the session id from the first `story-implement` envelope is still the authoritative one. Fix direction: surface the reused handle in every follow-up envelope so recovery doesn't need to walk back to the initial implementor result. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:178:  - Follow-up 3 (error-path guard + explicit member unavailability): `artifacts/06-.../009-continue.json` — added requestId guard to error catch paths + explicit memberId returns unavailable instead of fallback\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:189:  - (rd 2) explicit missing memberId silently falls back → **fixed** (continue 009: returns unavailable for explicit-but-missing member)\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:30:   * Runs `git clone` (or equivalent) for a source attachment. Returns `null`\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:41:   * Executes the bootstrap TS script in the working tree. Returns the child\n./apps/platform/server/routes/archive.ts:28:  turns: processArchiveTurnsApiPathnamePattern,\n./apps/platform/server/routes/archive.ts:127:    '/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns',\n./apps/platform/server/routes/archive.ts:145:        const turns = await app.turnDerivationService.getTurns({\n./apps/platform/server/routes/archive.ts:153:        return reply.code(200).send(turns);\n./tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts:75:  it('TC-1.2a returns only accessible projects sorted by lastUpdatedAt descending', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts:154:  it('returns an empty project list for an actor with no memberships', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts:221:  it('returns an empty shell bootstrap for an accessible project', async () => {\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:179:- fake Convex File Storage that returns predetermined markdown byte streams in response to signed URLs\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:182:- Mermaid library mock that records calls, returns controllable SVG fixtures, and simulates render failures\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:232:| TC-1.1a | `TC-1.1a bootstrap returns review workspace for process with reviewable artifact` | Process with one durable artifact version | GET bootstrap | response includes artifact in availableTargets |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:234:| TC-1.1d | `TC-1.1d multiple targets open in selection state` | Process with two targets, no selection | GET bootstrap | response returns availableTargets; `target` omitted |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:235:| TC-1.1e | `TC-1.1e zero-target direct route opens empty` | Process with zero targets | GET bootstrap | response returns empty availableTargets; `target` omitted |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:248:| `bootstrap returns 401 when unauthenticated` | Route-level auth invariant |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:249:| `bootstrap returns 404 PROCESS_NOT_FOUND for invalid processId` | Standard route failure path |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:268:| `returns unavailable when query versionId does not exist` | Robust input handling |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:269:| `returns unsupported content kind without attempting content fetch` | Efficiency + correctness for unsupported fallback |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:332:| `render error returns structured bodyStatus: error without throwing` | Bounded failure invariant |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:363:| TC-6.2c | `TC-6.2c revoked access on direct URL` | Bootstrap returns 403 | Mount page | route-level unavailable state |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:452:| `cache hit returns same SVG without re-calling mermaid.render` | LRU cache behavior |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:465:| TC-5.3a | `TC-5.3a export failure does not close review` | API returns 503 | Click export | failure affordance renders; surrounding panel remains operational |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:585:| `reopening with stale selection (deleted version) returns unavailable without leaking prior content` | Graceful degradation |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:600:| Export preparation (phase 1) begins within 2 s | `phase-1 POST returns within 2 s for 20-member package` | Call export route via `app.inject`; assert phase-1 response time under 2 s with Convex reads mocked at realistic fixture delay |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:700:**Scope:** `createPackageFromEntries` streaming API on the workspace package; tar hardening (gzip-bomb cap, per-entry + cumulative byte caps, entry-name filter, path-traversal rejection); two-phase export service (phase-1 POST returns signed URL JSON; phase-2 GET streams bytes); signed URL mint + verify; expired-URL 404; `mdvpkg` CLI polish; export trigger UI with download-link render; `_nav.md` manifest generation and round-trip.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:745:7. Select a prior version and confirm the body re-renders; confirm the URL updates via `history.pushState` so browser back returns to the prior selection.\n./tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts:552:  it('returns an unavailable selected member when an explicit memberId is missing', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts:668:  it('smoke returns a 20-member package review within the Story 4 timing target', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts:209:  it('TC-3.3b missing process archive read returns not found', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts:263:  it('invalid archive query returns INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST', async () => {\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:148:| `export.service.ts` | NEW | Two-phase export: POST returns `ExportPackageResponse` JSON with a signed download URL; GET at that URL (handled by the same `routes/review.ts` module) streams the `.mpkz` archive through `createPackageFromEntries` into the Fastify reply body | `PlatformStore`, `@liminal-build/markdown-package`, `export-url-signing` | AC-5 |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:299:- **`apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts`** — MODIFIED. Today this reader produces `ArtifactSummary` rows for the process work surface's materials envelope. Epic 4 extends its per-artifact projection to `getLatestArtifactVersion(artifactId)` and derive `currentVersionLabel` + `updatedAt` from that row. When the materials projection returns N artifacts, this costs N version-lookups; at first-cut material-list scale (≤ 20 items per process in Epic 2's NFR) this is acceptable. If a future epic materializes much larger materials lists, denormalization can be reintroduced as a performance optimization.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:618:Export is a **two-phase flow**. The POST `/export` endpoint returns a JSON metadata record with a signed GET download URL; the user's browser then GETs that URL to stream the `.mpkz` bytes. Expired URL retrieval returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:689:  }): Promise<string>;  // returns the new artifactVersionId\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:700:  }): Promise<string>;  // returns the new packageSnapshotId\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:759:The renderer never throws — it returns `bodyStatus: 'error'` with a populated `bodyError` when markdown parsing or sanitization fails. Mermaid sanitization is a pre-render step (fence interception inside the markdown-it pipeline) and cannot error the whole artifact; a malformed Mermaid source yields a non-empty `MermaidBlock` entry that the client will fail to render on its own.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:788:`requestExport` validates that every package member is available (otherwise `REVIEW_EXPORT_NOT_AVAILABLE`), mints a signed token via `export-url-signing.ts`, and returns the `ExportPackageResponse`. No bytes are streamed in this phase.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:790:`downloadExport` verifies the token (rejects expired or invalid tokens with 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`), re-validates the actor's access to the project/process, and returns a `Readable` that Fastify pipes into the reply body. Member content is streamed end-to-end via `createPackageFromEntries`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:805:  verify(token: string): ExportTokenPayload | null;  // returns null on invalid/expired\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:815:The review workspace bootstrap is the entry point from either the process work surface's `review` action or a direct URL reopen. The server resolves project and process access, computes reviewability, resolves the target from query state, and returns the workspace envelope in one durable read.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:868:| TC-1.1d | multiple targets open in selection state | `tests/service/server/review-workspace-api.test.ts` | process with two targets, no query state | response returns availableTargets only; `target` omitted |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:869:| TC-1.1e | zero-target direct route opens empty | `tests/service/server/review-workspace-api.test.ts` | process with zero targets, direct review URL | response returns empty availableTargets |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:875:| TC-6.2a | missing artifact shows unavailable | `tests/service/server/review-workspace-api.test.ts` | artifact deleted after URL bookmarked | response returns target with status: unavailable |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:883:Artifact review resolves the full version history for one artifact, selects either the query-state version or the current version as default, fetches the selected version's content from Convex File Storage, and renders it through the markdown pipeline. When an artifact exists in the current process review context but has no reviewable version yet, the artifact-specific endpoint still returns the artifact identity with an empty version list; the review-workspace wrapper later maps that condition to `target.status: empty`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:918:- if query state specifies a `versionId` that does not exist, the target-specific endpoint returns `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`; the **bootstrap** route is different and may still return a bounded `target.status: unavailable` workspace envelope when project/process context resolves\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:919:- `getArtifactVersionContentUrl` returns a Convex-issued stable URL (via `ctx.storage.getUrl()` wrapped in an `internalQuery`); Fastify fetches content over HTTP in the same request and does not cache the URL across requests. Access control lives at the route boundary\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:920:- content fetches time out at **`ARTIFACT_CONTENT_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000`** (exported as a constant from `artifact-review.service.ts` so tests can patch it); if the fetch times out or otherwise fails, the response returns `bodyStatus: 'error'` with `bodyError: { code: 'REVIEW_RENDER_FAILED', message: ... }` while keeping the version list visible\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:941:The render pipeline turns a markdown string into sanitized HTML with Mermaid placeholders, emitting the raw Mermaid sources in a sidecar list for client-side hydration. The pipeline is pure: it takes bytes in, returns a structured result, and does not touch any store or external system.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1010:4. Returns `{ blockId, sanitizedSource }` for the sidecar\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1049:Additional non-TC tests for this flow: mermaid directive stripping rejects `%%{init}%%` line, rejects `%%{config}%%` line, rejects `%%{wrap}%%` line; DOMPurify config rejects inline `<style>` tags; markdown-it `html: false` rejects raw `<script>` tags; render error path returns structured error without throwing.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1055:Package review resolves one published snapshot, returns the ordered member list, and fetches the selected member's artifact version detail through the same markdown render pipeline as Flow 2. A package member's `artifactVersionId` is the immutable pin — selecting a member always loads that specific version, never the artifact's current version. The snapshot is opened from one process review context, but its pinned members may come from multiple processes in the same project.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1110:| **A target is selected but has no reviewable inner content** | `target` is present with `target.status: 'empty'` | Artifact identity resolved but the artifact has zero `artifactVersions` rows; the artifact endpoint returns an empty version list and the workspace wrapper maps that to `target.status: 'empty'`, per AC-2.4 |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1134:Export is a two-phase flow. Phase 1 is a POST that validates the export request, mints a signed download URL, and returns metadata. Phase 2 is a GET at the signed URL that streams the `.mpkz` archive bytes through `@liminal-build/markdown-package`'s `createPackageFromEntries` into the Fastify reply body. Splitting the two phases matches the spec's `ExportPackageResponse` contract (with `downloadUrl` + `expiresAt`), lets the client render a real download link before bytes flow, and gives expired-URL handling (AC-5.3b) a natural implementation.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1208:- **Download URL reuse semantics.** The signed URL is **reusable within the expiry window** — the same URL can be GET'd multiple times until `expiresAt`, each GET re-validates the token, re-checks access + exportability, and streams a fresh archive. No single-use enforcement. This lets users copy the download link, re-download after an interrupted transfer, or share within the expiry if they choose. After `expiresAt`, every GET returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` regardless of how many prior downloads succeeded.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1211:- **Mid-stream auth.** If the actor's access to the project/process was revoked between phase 1 and phase 2, phase 2 returns 403 `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` at the start; no bytes stream.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1232:| TC-5.1a | export accepted and returns signed URL | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | exportable package | POST 200; response body is valid `ExportPackageResponse` with `downloadUrl`, `expiresAt`, `contentType: application/gzip`, `packageFormat: mpkz` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1233:| TC-5.1a (phase 2) | export download streams valid tar.gz | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | POST result's downloadUrl | GET returns 200 `application/gzip`; stream extracts to valid archive with expected members |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1235:| TC-5.1b (server-side) | preflight rejects when any member unavailable | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | package with unavailable member | POST returns 409 `REVIEW_EXPORT_NOT_AVAILABLE` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1239:| TC-5.3b | expired export requires re-export | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | signed URL with past `expiresAt` | GET returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1436:Members are listed in package order (by `position`). `parseManifest` returns a typed representation with `metadata.title`, `metadata.packageType`, `metadata.packageId`, `metadata.publishedAt` populated and all other `ManifestMetadata` fields absent; `scaffoldManifest` produces the markdown form from `{ snapshot, orderedMembers }` input.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1559:- Render error path returns structured error result rather than throwing\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1560:- Artifact review returns artifact identity plus `versions: []` for zero-version artifacts without attempting a content fetch; the workspace wrapper is what maps that condition to `target.status: empty`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1568:- `hasReviewableTargets` returns `false` for processes with zero artifact versions and zero package snapshots\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1569:- `hasReviewableTargets` returns `true` for processes with at least one reviewable target of either kind\n./tests/integration/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer-integration.test.ts:236:    it('updates an existing file and returns a new commit SHA distinct from the first commit', async () => {\n./tests/integration/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer-integration.test.ts:276:    it('returns a failed outcome with a meaningful failureReason when the target ref does not exist', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:101:  it('commits successfully to a writable target ref and returns the resulting commit SHA', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:137:  it('creates the file on first commit when getContent returns 404', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:151:  it('returns failed with a refresh-suggesting failureReason when GitHub responds 409 conflict', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:165:  it('returns failed naming the auth issue when GitHub returns 401', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:178:  it('returns failed naming the auth issue when GitHub returns 403', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:191:  it('returns failed describing the underlying network error when getContent throws a non-HTTP error', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:214:  it('returns failed when the repositoryUrl is not a github.com URL', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/octokit-code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:227:  it('returns failed when targetRef is null because direct write requires an explicit branch', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:135:  it('TC-2.1a returns the newest durable revision as the current version', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:586:  it('returns ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND when an explicit artifact version is unavailable', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:618:  it('TC-3.2b returns REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND when the process neither references nor pins the artifact', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:696:  it('TC-2.3b returns artifact versions newest to oldest', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:727:  it('TC-2.4a returns the no-version empty state for an owned artifact with no durable revisions', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:764:  it('TC-3.4c returns ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND when an explicit version is requested for a zero-version artifact', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:796:  it('returns a ready empty markdown review when a durable version body is zero-byte', async () => {\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md:223:| TC-3.4b | direct zero-version artifact review returns bounded empty state | Empty, not unavailable |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md:224:| TC-3.4c | explicit version request against zero-version artifact returns `ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND` | Exact request-level classification |\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:550:  it('returns PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE when start is attempted outside the draft state', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:570:  it('returns PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE when resume is attempted outside the paused or interrupted states', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:590:  it('returns PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE when respond is attempted outside a waiting state', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:907:  it('S2-TC-2.1a: start returns environment.state = preparing in the same session', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:971:  it('S2-TC-2.1b: resume returns environment.state = preparing when environment work is required', async () => {\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/code-checkpoint-writer.ts:10: * is not writable, the writer returns `outcome: 'failed'` with a meaningful\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/code-checkpoint-writer.ts:122:   * records calls and returns canned responses. Production omits this and the\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:253:  - When: User returns from review\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:254:  - Then: The user returns to that same process context\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:474:4. System returns export metadata for the reviewed package\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:494:  - Then: The platform returns a markdown package (`.mpkz`) export for that currently reviewed package\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:535:2. User reloads, leaves and returns later, or encounters unavailable review\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:629:Export is a two-phase flow. The POST endpoint returns export metadata including a signed download URL with a bounded expiry; the browser then follows that URL to a GET endpoint that streams the archive bytes.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:633:| Get process review workspace | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns the current review workspace bootstrap for one process |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:634:| Get artifact review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns review data for one artifact and its versions; optional query state may select one version |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:635:| Get package review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns review data for one output package; optional query state may select one member |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:636:| Request package export | POST | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}/export` | Phase 1 of export. Validates exportability, mints a signed download URL with bounded expiry, returns an `ExportPackageResponse` including `downloadUrl` and `expiresAt` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:637:| Download package export | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/exports/{exportId}` | Phase 2 of export. Consumes the signed token issued by the POST, re-verifies access and exportability, and streams the `.mpkz` archive as `application/gzip`. Returns `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` when the token is expired, tampered, or missing |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:773:member that cannot be reviewed still returns identity and an explanation\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:844:returns `target.status: unavailable` with `error.code:\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:138:  it('TC-3.1a returns populated shell section envelopes sorted by updatedAt descending', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:373:  it('TC-6.3a returns an artifact section error without blocking healthy sections', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:415:  it('returns project artifact summaries without legacy process ownership fields', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:568:  it('TC-6.3b returns a source section error without blocking healthy sections', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:610:  it('TC-6.3c returns a process section error without blocking healthy sections', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:689:  it('TC-6.2a returns 404 without leaking removed project data', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/script-execution.service.test.ts:76:  it(\"returns the provider's ExecutionResult unchanged\", async () => {\n./tests/service/server/daytona-provider-adapter.test.ts:163:  it('creates a sandbox and returns its id/workspace handle from ensureEnvironment', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:262:  it('TC-1.1a bootstrap returns environment state on first load', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:324:  it('TC-1.1b bootstrap returns explicit absent environment state for an early process', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:370:  it('TC-1.1g bootstrap returns stale environment truth from durable state', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:433:  it('bootstrap returns latest checkpoint visibility when one exists', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:1509:  it('returns stable section error envelopes without collapsing the whole surface', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:1580:  it('returns environment unavailable instead of collapsing the whole surface when the environment read fails', async () => {\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter-registry.ts:38: * Test-only registry that returns the same adapter for every `providerKind`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-server.md:229:  member set exactly, the mutation returns the existing row without creating a\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:8:  it('NullPlatformStore returns false because it has no durable recovery materials', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:16:  it('returns false when no materials, no outputs, and no sources are seeded', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:24:  it('returns false when seeded with empty arrays for refs and outputs', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:42:  it('returns true when at least one current artifact id exists', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:57:  it('returns true when at least one source attachment id exists', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:72:  it('returns true when at least one process output exists (no artifact refs)', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/nfr.test.ts:287:  it('returns a 20-member package review within 2 seconds', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:25:  it('FailingCodeCheckpointWriter returns a failed outcome with failureReason', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-html-routes.test.ts:115:  it('TC-6.4a missing process route returns a process unavailable shell', async () => {\n./tests/fixtures/archive.ts:244:  bodyText: 'Potential packing window for turns 0-1.',\n./tests/fixtures/archive.ts:274:  turns: [readyArchiveTurnFixture, degradedArchiveTurnFixture],\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:270:  - Then: The system returns a bounded unavailable result\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:286:list, but direct review access returns a bounded empty review state instead of\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:293:- **TC-3.4b: Zero-version direct review path returns empty state**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:302:  - Then: The system returns `ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND` rather than the\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:405:1. User returns later to a process work surface or review workspace\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:420:  - When: The user returns later to a process that still references that\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:425:  - When: The user returns later to review that package\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:485:| Get project shell | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:486:| Get process work surface | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:487:| Get review workspace | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns process-scoped review targets based on process reference and package context |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:488:| Get artifact review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:489:| Get package review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns one package with pinned member versions even when members were produced by multiple processes |\n./tests/service/server/review-workspace-api.test.ts:239:  it('TC-1.1e direct review route with zero targets returns the empty target state payload', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/project-create-api.test.ts:33:  it('TC-2.1a creates a project, assigns the owner, and returns an empty shell response', async () => {\n./tests/service/server/process-environment-fire-and-forget.test.ts:78:  // turns. Polling with a small sleep keeps the test stable.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states.md:131:context, the bootstrap stays `200` and returns `target.status: unavailable`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:63:The platform does not replace those inputs. It turns them into a coherent\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:276:and other managed views are later derived projections over turns.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:371:The user leaves and returns later. The project shell must restore enough state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:375:returns, the system restores the project, current processes, current artifact\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:682:**AC-31:** When the user returns after leaving a project, published process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:749:**AC-42:** The platform can derive turns from archived entries and later produce\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:750:chunks, summaries, and other managed views from those turns without mutating\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:780:  derived views over turns.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/01-review-entry-and-workspace-bootstrap.md:98:  - When: User returns from review\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/01-review-entry-and-workspace-bootstrap.md:99:  - Then: The user returns to that same process context\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:36:| Export response contract has `downloadUrl` and `expiresAt` fields that imply a two-phase export flow, but initial server-side Flow 5 design described a single-phase inline streaming response | Data Contracts → Export Package Response; AC-5 | **Two-phase flow.** POST `/api/.../packages/:packageId/export` returns 200 JSON `ExportPackageResponse` with a signed GET URL. Client renders a download link; user-initiated GET streams the `.mpkz` bytes. Expired URL retrieval returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`, matching TC-5.3b. | Resolved — clarified |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:71:Epic 4 is the first slice of Liminal Build's review layer. Epic 1 established the project shell, Epic 2 the process work surface, and Epic 3 the environment lifecycle and durable checkpointing that turns process-local work into canonical artifact state. What Epic 3 ends with is a process that can produce durable artifact outputs and code-change records — but those outputs are only visible as current-state projections on the process surface. You cannot yet open an artifact, read its body, compare it to a prior version, or bundle a set of artifacts as a reviewable output package. Epic 4 fills exactly that gap.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:81:The review surface itself is intentionally simpler than the process work surface: no live updates, no websocket subscription, no same-session reconciliation. A durable bootstrap returns the review workspace state, reopen restores durable state, and one failing review target degrades to a bounded failure envelope without taking down the rest of the surface. That simpler contract means the client work is significantly lighter than the process surface — no second live transport, no complex reconnect/sequence logic — which in turn makes room for the genuinely new surface concerns: markdown rendering, Mermaid hydration, version switching, and package navigation.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:161:`pnpm audit` remains broken in this repo because the underlying npm audit endpoint returns 410, and `npm audit` is not a valid substitute without a `package-lock.json`. Epic 3's tech design already flagged this; Epic 4 inherits the same limitation. Direct-dependency pressure testing via manual registry + advisory DB lookups is the current ceiling. A pnpm-compatible transitive-audit workflow should land before environment/runtime dependency work is treated as fully validated — tracked in Deferred Items alongside Epic 3's note.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:198:On the server, `markdown-it@14.1.1` is configured with `html: false` (stricter than MDV — we ingest agentic output, not user-authored files), extended with `@shikijs/markdown-it` (Shiki syntax highlighting), the vendored `markdown-it-anchor` (with the vendored `github-slugger`), and the purpose-built task-list renderer. Mermaid fences are intercepted: the server strips `%%{init}%%`, `%%{config}%%`, and `%%{wrap}%%` directives from each Mermaid source (closing the LobeChat/Docmost/OneUptime CVE class), then emits a placeholder div (`<div class=\"mermaid-placeholder\" data-block-id=\"...\"></div>`) into the rendered HTML and returns the sanitized Mermaid source as a sidecar entry in the `mermaidBlocks` array on the response. `isomorphic-dompurify@3.9.0` post-processes the rendered HTML with `USE_PROFILES: { html: true }` plus `FORBID_TAGS: ['style', 'math', 'form']`, `FORBID_ATTR: ['style']`, `ALLOW_DATA_ATTR: false`, `ALLOW_ARIA_ATTR: false`, and a narrow `ADD_ATTR: ['data-block-id']` allowlist for the Mermaid placeholder. SVG does not appear in the server-rendered HTML (Mermaid SVG is generated and sanitized client-side).\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:222:The failure boundary sits one level below the review workspace envelope. Request-level errors (401, 403, 404, 503) apply only to resolution and authorization — the response cannot be produced at all. Once project identity, process identity, and target identity resolve, the response always returns 200 with the review workspace envelope populated. Problems *inside* that envelope surface as bounded degraded states on specific fields:\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:286:| Review workspace bootstrap API | `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review` | Returns project + process + availableTargets + optional target for the selected review target |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:287:| Artifact review target API | `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/artifacts/:artifactId` | Returns one artifact's version list, selected version detail, and Mermaid sidecar |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:288:| Package review target API | `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/packages/:packageId` | Returns one package snapshot with members and the selected member's artifact detail |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:289:| Export package action | `POST /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/packages/:packageId/export` | Phase 1 of export: returns signed download metadata for a `.mpkz` archive; the subsequent GET to `/review/exports/:exportId` performs the actual byte stream |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:299:| File content retrieval via Convex File Storage URL | Fastify obtains a Convex-issued URL via `ctx.storage.getUrl()` and fetches content once per render — **the URL never leaves the Fastify process**. `ctx.storage.getUrl()` returns a URL whose storage ID is the sole credential (verified against Convex docs + maintainer guidance in get-convex/convex-backend#328 on 2026-04-17): the URL is fully public, does not expire, cannot be revoked short of blob deletion, and anyone who obtains it can fetch the content. Fastify therefore acts as an auth-proxy: it reads with the storage URL internally and streams bytes through its own authenticated route. Storage URLs are **never** returned in HTTP response bodies, never written to structured logs, never included in error payloads, and never visible to browser code |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:399:│   │   ├── export.service.ts                      # two-phase: POST returns signed URL JSON; GET streams bytes\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:528:| Chunk 5 | Package export (two-phase): streaming `createPackageFromEntries` in the workspace package; tar hardening (gzip-bomb cap, per-entry + cumulative byte caps, entry-name filter); Fastify POST export (returns signed-URL JSON) + GET download (streams bytes); signed URL mint + verify; expired-URL 404; unsupported-but-durable members remain exportable while unavailable members block export; `mdvpkg` CLI polish | AC-5.1 through AC-5.3 | export service, export-url-signing, `@liminal-build/markdown-package/tar/create-from-entries.ts`, export trigger UI |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:555:- **Export flow is two-phase**: POST `/api/.../packages/:packageId/export` returns 200 JSON with a signed GET URL and `expiresAt`. User's browser GETs the signed URL to stream the `.mpkz` bytes. Expired URL retrieval returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`. Matches the epic's `ExportPackageResponse` contract and TC-5.3b cleanly.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:560:- **Bootstrap error taxonomy**: review-workspace bootstrap returns a bounded `200` unavailable target state when project/process context resolves but the selected target no longer resolves in that context. Request-level `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` remains for target-specific endpoints and expired/tampered export-download URLs.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:36:history at low-level entry grain, from which turns, chunks, summaries, and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:84:| Archive | Fastify + Convex + cache/index layers | Full-fidelity low-level process history, turn derivation, later chunk/view derivation inputs | Processes | Canonical history is preserved at entry grain; turns and chunks are derived over it |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:171:| Full-fidelity archive entries are canonical while turns are derived | Context-management features can evolve without rewriting the archive |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:172:| Chunks summarize turns instead of replacing them | Derived views remain rebuildable from the archive |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:336:`Chunk` is a later derived grouping over one or more turns.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:342:**Consequence:** Archive entries carry the information needed to derive turns.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:576:  already-grouped turns or already-compressed summaries as canonical history.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/04-package-review-workspace.md:101:| Get package review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns review data for one output package; optional query state may select one member |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:6:- Current Story: 04-turn-derivation\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:33:- 04-turn-derivation\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:34:- 05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:185:- Story 4 owns deterministic turn derivation and cached rebuildable turn projections without mutating archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:186:- Story 5 owns non-summarizing structural derived views over turns, list/refresh routes, provenance to turns/archive entries, degraded/conflict behavior, and client rendering.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:27:- Zero-version direct review returns bounded empty state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:66:  - Then: The system returns a bounded unavailable result\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:79:**AC-3.4:** Zero-version artifacts are excluded from the default review target list, but direct review access returns a bounded empty review state instead of an unavailable error.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:85:- **TC-3.4b: Zero-version direct review path returns empty state**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:92:  - Then: The system returns `ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND` rather than the bounded empty zero-version state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:102:| Get review workspace | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns process-scoped review targets based on process reference and package context |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:103:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:62:| Get process review workspace | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns the current review workspace bootstrap for one process |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:63:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns review data for one artifact and its versions |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:64:| Get package review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns review data for one output package and its members |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:66:| Request package export | `POST` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}/export` | Validates exportability and returns signed download metadata for one reviewed package |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:51:  - When: The user returns later to a process that still references that artifact\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:55:  - When: The user returns later to review that package\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:99:| Get process work surface | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:100:| Get review workspace | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns process-scoped review targets based on process reference and package context |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:101:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:102:| Get package review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns one package with pinned member versions even when members were produced by multiple processes |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/01-project-artifact-association-without-process-ownership.md:85:| Get project shell | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/01-project-artifact-association-without-process-ownership.md:86:| Get process work surface | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:7:surfaces, turn derivation, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:20:| Client service tests | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts`, `tests/service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts`, `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | User-visible archive, turn, structural-view, empty, pagination, and degraded states |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:65:| TC-3.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.3b missing process archive read returns not found` | 404 `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:67:| TC-4.1a | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.1a turns derived from archive` | Entries grouped into turns |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:68:| TC-4.1b | `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | `TC-4.1b empty archive produces empty turn view` | Empty turns response |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:70:| TC-4.3a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-4.3a 