rived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-7.1b derived view restores after reload` | View readable or rebuilt |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:86:| TC-7.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-7.3a archive read returns bounded page` | Page has limit and next cursor |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:95:| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | same `processId + finalizationKey` returns or no-ops existing archive row | Primitive idempotency guard below Story 2 service proofs |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:97:| `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | turn-cache rebuild preserves stable turn provenance for derived views | Prevents dangling view references after rebuild |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:99:| `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | stale derived views are rebuilt from current turns without breaking archive reads | Covers rebuild consistency after new archive entries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:101:| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | derived-view refresh conflict returns `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Error contract coverage |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:102:| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | invalid archive query returns `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Error contract coverage |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:112:| 4 Turn derivation | 5 | 2 | 7 | turn derivation service |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:120:no-summary enforcement, stale/rebuilt derived views, primitive idempotency, atomic sequence\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:139:6. Open the turn view and verify turns reference source archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:140:7. Open derived views and verify structural turn ranges/chunk candidates have no generated summary text.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:8:history while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:31:entries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:41:| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:45:archive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:56:| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:61:| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:78:The design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:134:entries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:147:| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:176:├── turn-derivation.service.ts                # NEW: deterministic turn derivation and rebuild\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:190:├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:200:├── service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts    # NEW: deterministic turn derivation 