imately return request-level 404/409 responses | Data Contracts → Error Responses; AC-5.3, AC-5.4 | Design keeps the existing review-workspace bootstrap pattern: once project/process context resolves, `GET /review` returns `200` with bounded `target.status` / `target.error` degradation. Target-specific follow-up reads continue to use request-level `404` / `409` when the caller asks for an explicit missing version, missing member, or disallowed publication member | Resolved — clarified |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:30:only, leaves archive and derived views to Epic 7, and defers MCP/external-source\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:36:| Refresh cannot always settle synchronously | AC-3.3, Refresh Response | Design returns `refreshStatus: settled | pending | failed`, with pending as operation metadata rather than a fifth hydration state. | Resolved - clarified |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:52:| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:675:enrichment lookup fails, the reader returns durable source identity with\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:5:Expose non-summarizing structural derived views over turns with stable boundaries and provenance back to source turns and archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:12:- **Context:** The user is running or reviewing a process after source attachments, artifact versions, and source provenance have been established. The user needs to return later, inspect what happened, and trust that derived turns or chunks did not replace the original process record.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:18:Create the first derived-view layer over turns so later chunking, retrieval, summarization, and fidelity-gradient work can build from stable structural projections without replacing archive truth.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:44:- Story 4 turn derivation\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:52:**AC-5.1:** The platform can expose a non-summarizing structural derived view over one or more turns.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:55:  - Given: A process has derived turns\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:56:  - When: User requests a derived view\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:57:  - Then: The platform returns a derived view that identifies the turn boundary and does not require generated summary text\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:59:**AC-5.2:** Derived views identify structural boundaries for the turns they cover.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:62:  - Given: A derived view is returned for a turn range\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:6