facts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:293:| TC-6.3a | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.3a one failing source does not hide healthy sources` | Section returns healthy rows plus bounded error/degraded row |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:429:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts` defines `ImmediateSourceHydrationExecutor`, which always returns `{ kind: 'settled' }` with a fresh timestamp. `apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `DefaultSourceRefreshService` without supplying any other executor, so production always uses that stub. On every settled result, `refreshSource()` persists `hydrationState: 'hydrated'`, clears `freshnessReason`, and stamps `lastHydratedResolvedRef`/`lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` from GitHub even though no working-copy hydration or validation has happened. The only `working_copy_missing` references outside tests are a fixture and a condition check in `deriveHydrationState`, so the real app cannot detect or surface that recoverable stale case, and the pending/failed branches are only exercised through test doubles/fixtures rather than the runtime path.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:445:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts` defines `ImmediateSourceHydrationExecutor`, which always returns `{ kind: 'settled' }` with a fresh timestamp. `apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `DefaultSourceRefreshService` without supplying any other executor, so production always uses that stub. On every settled result, `refreshSource()` persists `hydrationState: 'hydrated'`, clears `freshnessReason`, and stamps `lastHydratedResolvedRef`/`lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` from GitHub even though no working-copy hydration or validation has happened. The only `working_copy_missing` references outside tests are a fixture and a condition check in `deriveHydrationState`, so the real app cannot detect or surface that recoverable stale case, and the pending/failed branches are only exercised through test doubles/fixtures rather than the runtime path.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/chunk-2-verification-codex.md:50:- If a future real remote adapter returns candidate refs that are not directly readable by the server, this should become a first-class contract method rather than a duck-typed extension.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/01-environment-state-and-visible-controls/sonnet-review.md:22:| TC-1.1a (server) | SATISFIED | HIGH | `process-work-surface-api.test.ts`: `TC-1.1a bootstrap returns environment state on first load` — asserts `environment.state = ready` and `controls` shape |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/01-environment-state-and-visible-controls/sonnet-review.md:23:| TC-1.1b (server) | SATISFIED | HIGH | `TC-1.1b bootstrap returns explicit absent environment state for an early process` — asserts `environment.state = absent` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/01-environment-state-and-visible-controls/sonnet-review.md:30:| TC-1.1g | SATISFIED | HIGH | `TC-1.1g stale state enables rehydrate and explains unavailable rebuild path` + server: `TC-1.1g bootstrap returns stale environment truth from durable state` (stale controls and bootstrap both tested) |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/01-environment-state-and-visible-controls/sonnet-review.md:45:| TC-1.5a (server) | SATISFIED | MEDIUM | Covered functionally by TC-1.1b test (process + materials present with absent env) and the `ThrowingEnvironmentSectionReader` test (returns 200 with process data + `unavailable` env); not named TC-1.5a. See COMPLETENESS_GAPS |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/01-environment-state-and-visible-controls/sonnet-review.md:56:| `tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts` | Added TC-1.1a (renamed), TC-1.1b (renamed), TC-1.1g, `bootstrap returns latest checkpoint visibility`, `returns environment unavailable instead of collapsing` | MATCHES claim — environment bootstrap and degradation tests present |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/01-environment-state-and-visible-controls/sonnet-review.md:164:2. **`deriveProcessSurfaceHasEnvironment` treats `unavailable` conditionally**: If `process.hasEnvironment` is true or `environmentId !== null`, `unavailable` still returns `true`. If neither, it returns `false`. This means an unavailable environment for a process that has never had one would return `hasEnvironment: false`, which is defensible but could surprise callers expecting `unavailable` to always imply a prior environment existed.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"f5ace4d9-f439-4a97-b702-83791b710d12\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/005-continue.json\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on convergence against the prior blocker in the runtime refresh path, plus the directly touched project-shell refresh surface and the new ambiguity called out by the implementor. Re-checked the production wiring, targeted refresh tests, and reran the story and epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-refresh-runtime-stub\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"The fake immediate-success default is gone. `DefaultSourceRefreshService` now requires an injected hydration executor, `createApp` wires a production `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor` through the real provider-adapter registry, and focused route tests prove refresh calls the provider seam and does not mark a source hydrated when runtime hydration fails.\"}],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project-shell refresh can still promise recovery for project-scoped stale/not-hydrated sources that the backend now rejects as not refreshable\",\"evidence\":\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project-shell refresh can still promise recovery for project-scoped stale/not-hydrated sources that the backend now rejects as not refreshable\",\"evidence\":\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1a\",\"TC-3.2b\",\"TC-3.3a\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts --environment node\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"For a project-scoped source shown in the project shell, what should refresh target when zero or multiple current processes reference that attachment: select/create a runtime target automatically, or hide/disable refresh until a single target exists?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The prior blocker is closed on the touched production path: settled refresh now depends on actual provider hydration/rehydration completion instead of an unconditional success stub.\",\"No new fake adapter or shim remains in runtime code for the refresh execution itself; the remaining issue is a product/scope decision about project-scoped refresh semantics and UI truthfulness.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:07:06.622Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:09:54.162Z\"}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:262:| TC-1.1a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-1.1a creates a project-scoped source attachment` | POST project route returns 201 summary |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:268:| TC-1.4a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-1.4a rejects invalid repository identity without partial row` | 