veHydrationState`, so the real app cannot detect or surface that recoverable stale case, and the pending/failed branches are only exercised through test doubles/fixtures rather than the runtime path.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:684:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts` defines `ImmediateSourceHydrationExecutor`, which always returns `{ kind: 'settled' }` with a fresh timestamp. `apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `DefaultSourceRefreshService` without supplying any other executor, so production always uses that stub. On every settled result, `refreshSource()` persists `hydrationState: 'hydrated'`, clears `freshnessReason`, and stamps `lastHydratedResolvedRef`/`lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` from GitHub even though no working-copy hydration or validation has happened. The only `working_copy_missing` references outside tests are a fixture and a condition check in `deriveHydrationState`, so the real app cannot detect or surface that recoverable stale case, and the pending/failed branches are only exercised through test doubles/fixtures rather than the runtime path.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:763:    planSummary: \"Replaced the fake immediate-refresh success path with a runtime-backed hydration executor that resolves a real process working-copy target, uses the provider adapter hydration/rehydration seam, returns pending/failed/not-available truthfully, and only marks a source hydrated after actual runtime refresh completion.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:806:      - \"Project-scoped refresh now requires exactly one current process working set to own the source attachment; if zero or multiple current processes reference it, the route returns SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE because Story 3 does not define a cross-process hydration target.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:868:        evidence: \"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:885:        evidence: \"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:921:      - \"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice4d-report.md:5:Verify and align the two client-facing page test cases (TC-2.1a/TC-2.5a and TC-2.1b/TC-2.5b) so that after a Start or Resume action returns, the environment panel immediately reflects `State: Preparing environment` — drawn from the action response fixture, not from a separate page reload.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"request-ruling\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The latest verifier resolved the prior production refresh-stub blocker but found a new blocking ambiguity: project-shell UI offers refresh for stale/not_hydrated project-scoped sources while the backend now rejects project-scoped refresh unless exactly one current process owns the working copy. The story-local requirements require refresh paths on project and process source surfaces, but do not define the target semantics for project-scoped refresh when zero or multiple processes reference the attachment. This is a product/scope decision, not a verifier or implementor guess.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"decisionType\\\":\\\"project-scoped-refresh-semantics\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"For project-scoped source attachments shown in the project shell, what should refresh do when the attachment is stale or not_hydrated but there is no single unambiguous current process working-copy target?\\\",\\\"defaultRecommendation\\\":\\\"Hide or disable the project-shell refresh control unless the backend can identify exactly one current process working-copy target; keep refresh enabled for process-scoped rows and for project-scoped rows with one unambiguous owning process. This avoids falsely promising recovery and aligns with AC-3.2 until a later story defines cross-process/project-level hydration semantics.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity is blocking and affects AC-3.2, AC-3.3, TC-3.2a, TC-3.2c, and TC-3.3a.\\\",\\\"Client project source section renders refresh controls for any stale or not_hydrated source regardless of scope.\\\",\\\"RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor returns SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source.\\\",\\\"All gates passed, but verifier outcome is needs-human-ruling because story-local requirements do not define project-scoped refresh target selection.\\\"],\\\"allowedResponses\\\":[\\\"Disable/hide project-shell refresh unless a single current process target exists; continue implementation to make UI truthful.\\\",\\\"Define project-scoped refresh to automatically select or create a runtime target; continue implementation with that behavior.\\\",\\\"Treat project-scoped refresh ambiguity as out of scope for Story 3 and allow current backend rejection despite the visible UI control.\\\",\\\"Block Story 3 until a separate design update defines project-scoped refresh semantics.\\\"]}}\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/007-story-orchestrate-status.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate status\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"single-attempt\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"single-attempt\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"storyRunId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHistoryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\",\"statusArtifactPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/progress/001-story-lead.status.json\",\"currentSnapshot\":{\"storyRunId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-mana