e` and `not_hydrated`.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:131:- Render pending refresh progress for the single source attachment without hiding the rest of the list.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:138:| Refresh orchestration and branch checks | `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`, `apps/platform/server/services/sources/github-repository-resolver.ts` |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:153:| TC-3.2a | `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts` | shows refresh action for stale source |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:156:| TC-3.3a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | refresh updates one source in place |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:157:| TC-3.3b | `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts` | shows refresh progress while pending |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:162:- `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`: request-level refresh errors differ from `refreshStatus: failed`\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:163:- `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`: pending refresh does not render as a fifth hydration state\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:168:- Keep pending refresh as operation metadata, not a hydration-state enum value.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:190:- Stale and not-yet-hydrated sources expose a refresh or hydration path\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:193:- Pending refresh does not appear as a fifth hydration state\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:36:| Refresh cannot always settle synchronously | AC-3.3, Refresh Response | Design returns `refreshStatus: settled | pending | failed`, with pending as operation metadata rather than a fifth hydration state. | Resolved - clarified |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:37:| Process-scoped shadowing needs exact read rule | Tech Design Question 7 | Design defines an active-source resolver that combines project-scoped and process-scoped attachments, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, and excludes detached rows. | Resolved |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:49:| 1 | What exact browser interaction model should attach, update, refresh, and detach use without creating a separate source-management app? | Extend the existing project shell and process work surface. Project-scoped actions appear in the project source section; process-scoped actions appear in the process materials/source area. Client calls Fastify JSON APIs and renders settled/pending/degraded responses in-place. No standalone source app or live source subscription is added. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:50:| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:51:| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:52:| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:54:| 6 | How should shell/process surfaces stay coherent across project and process scope? | Keep project shell source summaries for project-wide management. Process work surfaces show current sources after active-source resolution, including process-scoped shadowing and applicable project-scoped rows. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:70:attached, understand whether it can receive writes, refresh stale or missing\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:76:sandboxed filesystem is only a disposable working copy. Fastify is the source\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:78:process access, resolves shadowing rules, coordinates refresh, and records\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:147:| Environment refresh seam | Refresh/recovery paths | Epic 6 introduces a dedicated source refresh seam over existing process/environment services rather than assuming a full source-management implementation already exists |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:158:| Process-scoped attach updates current process source refs immediately | The epic says a process-scoped attachment belongs to one process as current source state and becomes visible immediately | `attachProcessSource` persists the source row and adds its id to that process's current source refs in the same orchestration path |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:159:| Process scope shadows project scope only in current-source reads | Same repo can be useful both project-wide and process-specific | Durable rows can coexist; resolver picks process-scoped row for that process when identity/ref collide |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:182:└── source-management.ts                         # NEW: Fastify routes for attach/update/refresh/detach/provenance\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:188:├── source-refresh.service.ts                 