,\"recommendedCurrentStory\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"recommendedCurrentPhase\":\"story-orchestrate\",\"continuationHandles\":{\"storyImplementor\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df47b-fba5-7480-915b-1ae2c61effc8\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"},\"storyVerifier\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"}},\"storyReceiptDraft\":{\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"storyTitle\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\",\"implementorEvidenceRefs\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/003-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/005-continue.json\"],\"verifierEvidenceRefs\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\"],\"gateCommand\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"gateResult\":\"pass\",\"dispositions\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"]}],\"baselineBeforeStory\":611,\"baselineAfterStory\":613,\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\"]},\"cumulativeBaseline\":{\"baselineBeforeCurrentStory\":611,\"expectedAfterCurrentStory\":613,\"latestActualTotal\":613},\"commitReadiness\":{\"state\":\"not-ready\",\"reason\":\"Caller ruling is still required before impl-lead commit.\"},\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\"]},\"cleanupHandoff\":{\"acceptedRiskItems\":[],\"deferredItems\":[{\"description\":\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null}],\"cleanupRequired\":true},\"rulingRequest\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001-ruling-018\",\"decisionType\":\"project-scoped-refresh-semantics\",\"question\":\"For project-scoped source attachments shown in the project shell, what should refresh do when the attachment is stale or not_hydrated but there is no single unambiguous current process working-copy target?\",\"defaultRecommendation\":\"Hide or disable the project-shell refresh control unless the backend can identify exactly one current process working-copy target; keep refresh enabled for process-scoped rows and for project-scoped rows with one unambiguous owning process. This avoids falsely promising recovery and aligns with AC-3.2 until a later story defines cross-process/project-level hydration semantics.\",\"evidence\":[\"Verifier finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity is blocking and affects AC-3.2, AC-3.3, TC-3.2a, TC-3.2c, and TC-3.3a.\",\"Client project source section renders refresh controls for any stale or not_hydrated source regardless of scope.\",\"RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor returns SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source.\",\"All gates passed, but verifier outcome is needs-human-ruling because story-local requirements do not define project-scoped refresh target selection.\"],\"allowedResponses\":[\"Disable/hide project-shell refresh unless a single current process target exists; continue implementation to make UI truthful.\",\"Define project-scoped refresh to automatically select or create a runtime target; continue implementation with that behavior.\",\"Treat project-scoped refresh ambiguity as out of scope for Story 3 and allow current backend rejection despite the visible UI control.\",\"Block Story 3 until a separate design update defines project-scoped refresh semantics.\"]},\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"ask-ruling\"},\"startedFromPrimitiveArtifacts\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/001-story-validate.json\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"story-run-current\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-current.json\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-events\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-final-package\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-final-package.json\"},{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/002-story-orchestrate-run.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T19:34:03.502Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:10:05.331Z\"}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice7-run.json:3:  \"result\": \"Done. 25/25 tests pass.\\n\\n**What changed:**\\n\\n- `WorkingSetPlan` gains `outputIds: string[]`\\n- `planHydrationWorkingSet` now accepts `HydrationWorkingSetInput` (material refs + `outputIds`) and returns all three arrays\\n- Both start and resume services parallel-fetch `listProcessOutputs` alongside `getCurrentProcessMaterialRefs` when entering preparation, then pass the combined input to the planner\\n- TC-2.2a proves output IDs flow into the plan when present (start path); TC-2.2b proves an empty `outputIds: []` is stored cleanly when no outputs exist (resume path)\\n- HC-1/2/3 updated to include `outputIds: []` to satisfy `toEqual` exact matching\",\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/nitfix-sonnet-review.md:25:| 14 | `hasCanonicalRecoveryMaterials` real check | Yes — replaced unconditional `true` with `getCurrentProcessMaterialRefs` check: returns `true` iff `artifactIds.length > 0 || sourceAttachmentIds.length > 0` | Yes — covered indirectly by integration and action tests; no dedicated unit test, but the logic is a one-liner backed by an existing method |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice1-run.json:3:  \"result\": \"All 20 tests pass. Here's what was implemented:\\n\\n**`process-start.service.ts`** — already upserted to `preparing`, but wasn't passing `environment` in the response. Now conditionally upserts only when the result status is `running`/`waiting` (skips for terminal results), and includes `environment` in `startProcessResponseSchema.parse()`.\\n\\n**`process-resume.service.ts`** — previously only read env, never transitioned it. Now fetches the existing env, then upserts to `preparing` (preserving `environmentId` + `lastHydratedAt`) when the result process is `running` or `waiting`. Includes `environment` in the response.\\n\\n**`process-actions-api.test.ts`** — 5 new tests added covering:\\n- S2-TC-2.1a: start returns `environment.state = preparing` in the same session + bootstrap durability\\n- S2-TC-2.1b: resume returns preparing when env is absent + preserves hydration context from prior `ready` env\\n- S2-TC-2.4b: terminal start result does not enter preparing state\\n- Updated existing \\\"resume always enters preparing\\\" test to assert the correct preparing-state disabled reasons\\n\\nReport written to `story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice1-report.md`.\",\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/chunk-1-verification-codex-r2.md:44:- `convex/processes.ts:264-318` now inserts the env-state row, inserts the per-process-type state row, computes `initialFingerprint = await computeWorkingSetFingerprint(ctx, processId)`, and patches the env-state row with that value before the mutation returns.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice2-report.md:13:  Returns a spread of `defaultEnvironmentSummary` with the caller-supplied `state`, `environmentId`, `blockedReason`, and `lastHydratedAt`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice4-report.md:9:Server already returns `environment: { state: 'preparing' }` for running/waiting outcomes\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/codex-review.md:20:| TC-5.5a | VIOLATED | OBSERVED: `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:120-129`, `854-879`, `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:761-779`, `tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:1340-1369`, `tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts:1055-1086` | The test proves the behavior with `InMemoryPlatformStore`, but `isCanonicalRecoveryMaterialSetExplicitlyMissing()` explicitly returns `false` for non-Map-backed stores, making the required `422 PROCESS_ENVIRONMENT_PREREQUISITE_MISSING` unreachable in production. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/codex-review.md:63:- finding: `PROCESS_ENVIRONMENT_PREREQUISITE_MISSING` is only reachable in the in-memory test store because prerequisite detection inspects test-only Maps and returns `false` for the real Convex store.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:22:  - `process-work-surface-api.test.ts`: bootstrap returns `environment.state = stale` distinctly (TC-5.1a server test confirmed from test-plan mapping).\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:27:  - `process-work-surface-api.test.ts`: bootstrap returns `environment.state = lost` distinctly.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:38:  - `process-actions-api.test.ts`: POST `/rehydrate` on stale environment returns 200 and triggers `InMemoryProviderAdapter.rehydrateEnvironment`. Evidence: `assertRehydrateAvailable` allows `state === 'stale' && environmentId !== null`; route handler delegates to `processEnvironmentService.rehydrate`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:47:  - `process-actions-api.test.ts`: POST `/rebuild` on lost environment returns 200, provider `rebuildEnvironment` called. `assertRebuildAvailable` allows `state === 'lost'`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:64:  - `process-work-surface-page.test.ts`: `TC-5.5a rebuild blocked by missing canonical prerequisite keeps the blocked recovery reason visible on the surface` — 422 response renders `actionError`, no false ready state. Route returns 422/`PROCESS_ENVIRONMENT_PREREQUISITE_MISSING` from `assertRebuildAvailable` / `hasCanonicalRecoveryMaterials` check.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:102:**`isCanonicalRecoveryMaterialSetExplicitlyMissing` guard:** The prerequisite-missing check uses duck-typed internal store map access. This is intentional for the test-only path (the guard returns false for production stores that don't expose these internal maps), making it exclusively a test-harness behavioral control. Not a concern for correctness.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
