a9d-ae78-860601218c19\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df43c-e0a0-7302-a4ed-61ebb6077974\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df43c-e0a0-7302-a4ed-61ebb6077974\",\"storyId\":\"01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Attach Repositories to a Project or Process\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/005-continue.json\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-composer.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/app/shell-app.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/browser-api/projects-api.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/browser-api/process-work-surface-api.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/project-shell-page.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/process-materials-section.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on closing SV-01 and SV-02 by checking the newly added project/process attach UI actions, browser API wiring, immediate surface refresh behavior, and the expanded process current-source contract/rendering. I also re-checked the Story 1 regression evidence for duplicate blocking, null-target duplicate handling, invalid/inaccessible no-partial-row rejection, and process current-source mutation, then reran the story and epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"SV-01\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"The project shell and process work surface now both expose real attach forms via the shared composer (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-composer.ts:15-127), wired into the project shell and process work-surface renderers (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts:14-58, apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts:83-101, apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:48-70, apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:214-228). Bootstrap now calls the real POST routes through browser API wrappers and immediately refetches the active shell/surface after create (apps/platform/client/browser-api/projects-api.ts:108-127, apps/platform/client/browser-api/process-work-surface-api.ts:233-256, apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:1636-1709). Client tests cover the project-shell and process-surface attach submissions (tests/service/client/project-shell-page.test.ts:125-180, tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts:559-602).\"},{\"id\":\"SV-02\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"Process currentSources now carry repositoryFullName and attachmentScope in the shared contract (apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:319-333), the materials reader projects both fields from durable source attachments (apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:80-101), and the process materials UI renders Repository and Scope details for each current source (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:236-253). The refreshed process attach API expectation now requires both fields after create (tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:222-236), and client rendering tests assert that the process surface shows repository identity and scope (tests/service/client/process-materials-section.test.ts:45-57, tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts:537-557).\"}],\"newFindings\":[],\"openFindings\":[],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\",\"TC-1.2a\",\"TC-1.3a\",\"TC-1.3b\",\"TC-1.3c\",\"TC-1.4a\",\"TC-1.4b\"],\"unverified\":[]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"pass\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The regression evidence remains intact: duplicate exact attachment blocking is still covered in tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:241-285, missing-target-ref duplicate handling is still covered in convex/sourceAttachments.test.ts:288-327, invalid/inaccessible no-partial-row rejection is still covered in tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:288-360, and process current-source mutation is still evidenced by tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:182-238.\",\"The story markdown still contains a documentation-level contract ambiguity: the Create Response table describes a {\\\"sourceAttachment\\\": ...} wrapper, while Flow 1, the route schemas, browser API wrappers, and tests all use a bare SourceAttachmentSummary. I did not treat that as blocking because the implemented/server-tested contract is internally consistent and the required gates passed.\",\"Epic gate output still shows the repo-baseline e2e scaffold message (test:e2e prints SKIP), which did not block verify-all.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/006-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T18:41:09.023Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T18:43:11.315Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"866dbbbb-6953-475f-8385-71ab8f428992\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"AGENTS.md\",\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/routes/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts\",\"tests/fixtures/sources.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Reviewed Story 3 hydration/freshness behavior across the Fastify refresh route, refresh orchestration, project/process source readers, shared contracts, client source surfaces, fixtures, and mapped server/client tests, then ran targeted tests plus the story and epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-refresh-runtime-stub\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production refresh is wired to a fake immediate-success executor instead of a real rehydration path\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts` defines `ImmediateSourceHydrationExecutor`, which always returns `{ kind: 'settled' }` with a fresh timestamp. `apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `DefaultSourceRefreshService` without supplying any other executor, so production always uses that stub. On every settled result, `refreshSource()` persists `hydrationState: 'hydrated'`, clears `freshnessReason`, and stamps `lastHydratedResolvedRef`/`lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` from GitHub even though no working-copy hydration or validation has happened. The only `working_copy_missing` references outside tests are a fixture and a condition check in `deriveHydrationState`, so the real app cannot detect or surface that recoverable stale case, and the pending/failed branches are only exercised through test doubles/fixtures rather than the runtime path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3a\",\"TC-3.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-refresh-runtime-stub\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production refresh is wired to a fake immediate-success executor instead of a real rehydration path\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts` defines `ImmediateSourceHydrationExecutor`, which always returns `{ kind: 'settled' }` with a fresh timestamp. `apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `DefaultSourceRefreshService` without supplying any other executor, so production always uses that stub. On every settled result, `refreshSource()` persists `hydrationState: 'hydrated'`, clears `freshnessReason`, and stamps `lastHydratedResolvedRef`/`lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` from GitHub even though no working-copy hydration or validation has happened. The only `working_copy_missing` references outside tests are a fixture and a condition check in `deriveHydrationState`, so the real app cannot detect or surface that recoverable stale case, and the pending/failed branches are only exercised through test doubles/fixtures rather than the runtime path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3a\",\"TC-3.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1a\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2b\",\"TC-3.2c\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3a\",\"TC-3.3b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The runtime refresh endpoint is not backed by a real hydration/rehydration seam: by default it always records an immediate settled success, so production cannot truthfully produce in-flight pending/failed refresh behavior or prove that a stale/not-hydrated working copy was actually refreshed.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Automated coverage is good for state labels, branch-drift stale detection, refresh button visibility, and route contracts, but those checks still pass because pending/failed flows are simulated with fixtures or injected test doubles rather than exercised through the real production executor path.\",\"The onboarding docs path referenced in `AGENTS.md` (`docs/onboarding/`) was not present in this checkout, so baseline context came from the story, tech design, test plan, and implementation/tests directly.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T19:53:24.228Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T19:59:35.895Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/011-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"56d5bd1a-7866-4b48-ab5b-dca6a9d87344\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df66a-060e-7fd1-906a-9cee34ec3e12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df66a-060e-7fd1-906a-9cee34ec3e12\",\"storyId\":\"02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Finalization Boundary Between Live State and Archive\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"convex/processHistoryItems.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\",\"tests/fixtures/archive.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Reviewed Story 2 against its story/spec/test-plan, then verified the finalization seam across `ArchiveFinalizationService`, the user-response and execution hooks, process-history compatibility, and the Story 2 server/client tests. I also ran the configured story and epic gates plus an ad hoc runtime reproduction of execution-result archiving.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-02-history-bridge-identity-mismatch\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Execution-result archive rows are keyed to transient provider IDs instead of the persisted live history items\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-02-history-bridge-identity-mismatch\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Execution-result archive rows are keyed to transient provider IDs instead of the persisted live history items\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"TC-2.1a\",\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2a\",\"TC-2.2b\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run test:service -- --run tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The real execution-result hook archives the pre-persistence provider object instead of the persisted `processHistoryItems` row, so production archive identity diverges from the live-history identity even though duplicate suppression still passes.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but the current Story 2 tests miss the identity mismatch because TC-2.3b asserts the provider-supplied `runtime-model-1` ID rather than the stored history row returned by `appendProcessHistoryItem`.\",\"Live/archive separation itself is otherwise evidenced well: `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:306-372` and `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:243-274` both show websocket/reducer history upserts do not create archive rows.\",\"I did not find a fake adapter or placeholder branch wired into the runtime finalization path; the blocking issue is a real production data-link mismatch in the execution completion hook.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/011-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T04:33:56.521Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T04:41:26.481Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/008-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"0e9a8687-385a-4fea-910a-53a721965ff0\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df617-f545-7c12-973a-19e600231531\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df617-f545-7c12-973a-19e600231531\",\"storyId\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Canonical Archive Entry Persistence\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/004-implementor.json\",\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\",\"convex/schema.ts\",\"convex/test_helpers/fake_convex_context.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Reviewed Story 1 against AC-1.1 through AC-1.4, including the Convex archive entry mutation/query, schema and PlatformStore wiring, shared archive contracts, documented TC mappings, the local test harness, and the configured story/epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S1-F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Story 1 scope and evidence requirements conflict, leaving AC-1.1 and AC-1.4 unproven\",\"evidence\":\"The story scope explicitly defers live finalization hooks, archive read routes/UI, and read-time provenance enrichment to later stories (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:36-38`, `174-178`), but the same story still requires TC-1.1a/b/c and TC-1.4a/b coverage (`.../01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:156-166`, `192-199`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:36-44`). Those mapped files do not exist (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`), `rg` found no `ArchiveFinalizationService`/`appendFinalizedEntry` or `ArchiveReadService`/`getArchive` implementation under `apps/platform/server/services`, and the only executable proof is the Convex handler test (`convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:196-236`, `370-436`). That leaves finalized user/model/process-event archival and degraded related-context reads without the required story-level evidence.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\",\"TC-1.1c\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.4a\",\"TC-1.4b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S1-F2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"The production archive read path paginates after loading the full process archive\",\"evidence\":\"`listArchiveEntries` reads `by_processId_and_sequence` with `.collect()` and only then slices in `paginateArchiveEntries` (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:139-155`, `261-280`). The story/design describe this store method as returning one bounded page (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:126-127`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:661-668`). The outward page contract is correct, but long-process production reads still materialize the full archive in memory.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S1-F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Story 1 scope and evidence requirements conflict, leaving AC-1.1 and AC-1.4 unproven\",\"evidence\":\"The story scope explicitly defers live finalization hooks, archive read routes/UI, and read-time provenance enrichment to later stories (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:36-38`, `174-178`), but the same story still requires TC-1.1a/b/c and TC-1.4a/b coverage (`.../01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:156-166`, `192-199`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:36-44`). Those mapped files do not exist (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`), `rg` found no `ArchiveFinalizationService`/`appendFinalizedEntry` or `ArchiveReadService`/`getArchive` implementation under `apps/platform/server/services`, and the only executable proof is the Convex handler test (`convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:196-236`, `370-436`). That leaves finalized user/model/process-event archival and degraded related-context reads without the required story-level evidence.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\",\"TC-1.1c\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.4a\",\"TC-1.4b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S1-F2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"The production archive read path paginates after loading the full process archive\",\"evidence\":\"`listArchiveEntries` reads `by_processId_and_sequence` with `.collect()` and only then slices in `paginateArchiveEntries` (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:139-155`, `261-280`). The story/design describe this store method as returning one bounded page (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:126-127`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:661-668`). The outward page contract is correct, but long-process production reads still materialize the full archive in memory.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-1.2\",\"TC-1.2a\",\"TC-1.2b\",\"AC-1.3\",\"TC-1.3a\",\"TC-1.3b\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\",\"TC-1.1c\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.4a\",\"TC-1.4b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm exec vitest run convex/archiveEntries.test.ts --environment node\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`convex/archiveEntries.ts:139-155` uses `collect()` plus in-memory slicing for `listArchiveEntries`, so long-process archive reads are not yet bounded at the persistence layer.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"Should Story 1 be accepted on primitive-only evidence, or are TC-1.1 and TC-1.4 intentionally still in-scope despite the scope notes that defer finalization hooks, archive API, and provenance enrichment to Stories 2, 3, and 6?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder branch, or compatibility workaround was found in the inspected production archive persistence path; the runtime path is the real Convex mutation/query plus the real ConvexPlatformStore call-through.\",\"Both configured gates passed locally; the remaining blockers are requirement/scope proof gaps rather than format, lint, type, build, or test failures.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/008-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T03:04:18.275Z\",\"finishedAt\":