ummary unchanged (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts`), and the process materials reader still emits `lastHydratedAt` / `freshnessReason` whenever present (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts`). The shared project contract also requires `lastHydratedResolvedRef` and `lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` on every source row (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts`), so unavailable rows returned from real GET surfaces can still expose prior hydration details. The only new TC-6.2a proof is a synthetic UI-envelope test (`tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`), which means the route/read path required by the story’s anti-shim rule is not actually proving redaction.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-06-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unavailable source reads still serialize stale hydration metadata\",\"evidence\":\"`buildUnavailableSourceAttachment` only flips availability-related fields and leaves prior hydration metadata on the summary (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The project-shell reader forwards that summary unchanged (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts`), and the process materials reader still emits `lastHydratedAt` / `freshnessReason` whenever present (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts`). The shared project contract also requires `lastHydratedResolvedRef` and `lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` on every source row (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts`), so unavailable rows returned from real GET surfaces can still expose prior hydration details. The only new TC-6.2a proof is a synthetic UI-envelope test (`tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`), which means the route/read path required by the story’s anti-shim rule is not actually proving redaction.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1a\",\"TC-6.1b\",\"TC-6.2b\",\"AC-6.3\",\"TC-6.3a\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2a\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Real project/process read APIs still rely on client-side hiding for unavailable-source redaction; the runtime payloads can carry prior hydration metadata for degraded rows.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Focused story tests also passed: `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`.\",\"`docs/onboarding/current-state-index.md`, `current-state-tech-design.md`, and `current-state-code-map.md` referenced by `AGENTS.md` were not present in this checkout, so this review used the story/spec docs directly.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T23:15:18.535Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T23:20:47.580Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"f5ace4d9-f439-4a97-b702-83791b710d12\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/005-continue.json\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on convergence against the prior blocker in the runtime refresh path, plus the directly touched project-shell refresh surface and the new ambiguity called out by the implementor. Re-checked the production wiring, targeted refresh tests, and reran the story and epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-refresh-runtime-stub\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"The fake immediate-success default is gone. `DefaultSourceRefreshService` now requires an injected hydration executor, `createApp` wires a production `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor` through the real provider-adapter registry, and focused route tests prove refresh calls the provider seam and does not mark a source hydrated when runtime hydration fails.\"}],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project-shell refresh can still promise recovery for project-scoped stale/not-hydrated sources that the backend now rejects as not refreshable\",\"evidence\":\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project-shell refresh can still promise recovery for project-scoped stale/not-hydrated sources that the backend now rejects as not refreshable\",\"evidence\":\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1a\",\"TC-3.2b\",\"TC-3.3a\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts --environment node\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"For a project-scoped source shown in the project shell, what should refresh target when zero or multiple current processes reference that attachment: select/create a runtime target automatically, or hide/disable refresh until a single target exists?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The prior blocker is closed on the touched production path: settled refresh now depends on actual provider hydration/rehydration completion instead of an unconditional success stub.\",\"No new fake adapter or shim remains in runtime code for the refresh execution itself; the remaining issue is a product/scope decision about project-scoped refresh semantics and UI truthfulness.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:07:06.622Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:09:54.162Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/010-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"fcb5202c-4d3c-4874-baa5-c7b50776685e\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/009-continue.json\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on the prior project-shell refresh ambiguity finding. Re-checked the new project refresh-target-count contract, the project shell reader/UI gating, the touched refresh runtime, the focused client/server tests, and reran the story and epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"Project source summaries now expose `projectRefreshTargetCount`, `SourceSectionReader` computes that count from current process material refs, and the project-shell UI only renders refresh/hydrate controls for process-scoped sources or project-scoped sources with exactly one current target. Focused UI tests cover zero/one/many target cases, focused bootstrap API tests verify the summary metadata contract, and the story/epic gates both pass.\"}],\"newFindings\":[],\"openFindings\":[],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.1a\",\"TC-3.2a\",\"TC-3.2b\",\"TC-3.2c\",\"TC-3.3a\",\"TC-3.3b\"],\"unverified\":[]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm exec vitest run tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts --environment node\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"pass\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The touched production path no longer presents the false project-shell recovery affordance from the prior verifier finding: ambiguous project-scoped rows keep their hydration/freshness visibility but do not offer refresh until ownership is unambiguous.\",\"No new fake adapter, shim, or placeholder behavior was found in the tou